WEBVTT

00:00.839 --> 00:04.039
[upbeat ukulele music]
[欢快的尤克里里音乐]

00:04.039 --> 00:10.572
*
*
*
*
*
*
*
*

00:10.572 --> 00:13.039
- [panting]
- [气喘吁吁]

00:18.872 --> 00:20.905
- All right, hold on a second,
you freeloader.
- 好吧，等一下，
你这个贪图便宜的人。

00:20.905 --> 00:21.905
What are you doing here?
你在这里做什么？

00:21.905 --> 00:23.472
- I'm here for lunch.
- 我来这里吃午饭。

00:23.472 --> 00:26.039
- Did you bring money
this time?
- 你带钱了吗
这次？

00:26.039 --> 00:27.205
- Yes.
- 是的。

00:27.205 --> 00:29.905
- [panting and barking]
- [喘气和吠叫]

00:29.905 --> 00:32.805
Let me see that.
[sniffs]
让我看看。
[嗅嗅]

00:38.872 --> 00:41.772
All right, tastes real.
Now get in line.
不错，味道正宗。
现在排队吧。

00:41.772 --> 00:45.739
- Yes, sir.
- 是的，先生。

00:45.739 --> 00:48.539
- Hey, how's that new Executive
Treatment sandwich treating you?
- 嘿，那个新主管怎么样
治疗三明治治疗你吗？

00:48.539 --> 00:51.572
'Cause it's hitting all the
quadrants of my hunger markets.
因为它击中了所有
我的饥饿市场的象限。

00:51.572 --> 00:53.972
- Mmm, quadrants.
- 嗯，象限。

00:53.972 --> 00:55.472
- You know, it reminds me
of something I was saying
- 你知道，这让我想起了
我正在说的事情

00:55.472 --> 00:57.105
about business the other day.
前几天谈生意。

00:57.105 --> 01:00.172
- The satisfaction earnings of
the fourth quarter of my lunch
- 满意度收入
我的午餐的第四季度

01:00.172 --> 01:01.805
are off the charts.
都破纪录了。

01:01.805 --> 01:02.905
[laughter]
[笑声]

01:02.905 --> 01:05.472
- And I love the way
it tastes.
- 我喜欢这种方式
它的味道。

01:05.472 --> 01:06.739
- And business, my friend,
- 还有生意，我的朋友，

01:06.739 --> 01:08.339
is the business
that I'm talking about.
是生意
我正在谈论的。

01:08.339 --> 01:11.472
- Well, one can't have business
without business, right?
- 好吧，一个人不能做生意
没有生意，对吗？

01:11.472 --> 01:14.439
- Interesting point, Marv.
How's your sandwich?
- 有趣的一点，马夫。
你的三明治怎么样？

01:14.439 --> 01:16.039
- Absolutely spectacular.
- 绝对壮观。

01:16.039 --> 01:17.905
This new menu item is
a business plan
这个新菜单项是
商业计划

01:17.905 --> 01:20.405
I can really get behind.
我真的可以落后。

01:20.405 --> 01:23.372
- I tell you, this is one
dynamic little sandwich.
- 我告诉你，这是一个
充满活力的小三明治。

01:23.372 --> 01:25.472
- With levels of proactiveness
that are off the charts,
- 具有积极主动性
那些超出图表的，

01:25.472 --> 01:26.905
business-wise.
商业方面。

01:26.905 --> 01:28.739
- It really appeals
to my demographic.
- 真的很吸引人
就我的人口统计而言。

01:28.739 --> 01:30.339
- Well, you are an executive
- 嗯，你是一名高管

01:30.339 --> 01:31.905
in the fast-paced
world of business.
在快节奏的
商业世界。

01:31.905 --> 01:33.872
- Ha ha!
That's for sure.
- 哈哈！
这是肯定的。

01:33.872 --> 01:35.539
- These guys talk funny words.
- 这些家伙说着有趣的话。

01:35.539 --> 01:38.905
- Oh, yeah, they're a riot.
What can I get you?
- 哦，是的，他们很骚乱。
我能给你什么？

01:38.905 --> 01:42.005
- I guess I'll have one
of these business sandwiches
- 我想我会拥有一个
这些商务三明治

01:42.005 --> 01:43.739
everybody's talking about.
每个人都在谈论。

01:43.739 --> 01:47.505
- Ah, the Executive Treatment.
- Is that what you call it?
- 啊，行政待遇。
- 你就是这么称呼它的吗？

01:47.505 --> 01:50.505
- Well, that's what
Mr. Krabs makes me call it.
- 嗯，就是这样
蟹老板让我给它打电话。

01:50.505 --> 01:53.439
It's really just a Krabby Patty
that costs more,
这真的只是一个蟹肉饼
那样花费更多，

01:53.439 --> 01:57.505
and SpongeBob wears a different
tie when he makes it.
海绵宝宝穿着不同的
当他成功时打领带。

01:57.505 --> 01:59.605
- Oh, wow.
I'll take seven.
- 哦，哇。
我要七个。

01:59.605 --> 02:01.205
- Oh, I'm sorry, sir.
- 哦，对不起，先生。

02:01.205 --> 02:04.839
The executive treatment is
available to executives only.
行政待遇是
仅适用于高管。

02:04.839 --> 02:06.405
I'm not sorry.
我不后悔。

02:06.405 --> 02:10.139
- But I've never wanted anything
so much in my whole life
- 但我从来没有想要过任何东西
我一生中就这么多

02:10.139 --> 02:12.605
since this morning
when I wanted a doughnut
从今天早上开始
当我想要一个甜甜圈时

02:12.605 --> 02:14.172
and I ate that doughnut
我吃了那个甜甜圈

02:14.172 --> 02:17.939
and it was great.
太棒了。

02:17.939 --> 02:20.972
That doughnut is gone.
那个甜甜圈不见了。

02:20.972 --> 02:22.839
The doughnut is gone!
甜甜圈不见了！

02:22.839 --> 02:27.172
- First of all, a lot of that
doughnut is still on your face.
- 首先，很多
甜甜圈还在你脸上。

02:28.572 --> 02:31.905
- Now, where's
my Executive Treatment?
- 现在，在哪里
我的行政待遇？

02:31.905 --> 02:34.739
- I told you,
it's for executives only.
- 我告诉过你，
仅供高管使用。

02:34.739 --> 02:38.005
And you aren't even dressed
like an executive.
而你连衣服都没穿
就像一个行政人员。

02:38.005 --> 02:39.739
I could, of course, sell you
我当然可以卖给你

02:39.739 --> 02:44.305
an official Krusty Krab
business tie for only $10.
官方的蟹堡王
商务领带仅需 10 美元。

02:44.305 --> 02:46.839
- Will the tie let me order
the Executive Treatment?
- 领带可以让我订购吗
行政待遇？

02:46.839 --> 02:51.439
- Not on its own, no, but you
could Krabby-size the tie
- 不是靠它自己，不，而是靠你
Krabby 可以调整领带的尺寸吗

02:51.439 --> 02:53.772
and get a set
of business glasses
并获得一套
商务眼镜

02:53.772 --> 02:55.739
for an additional $10.
额外支付 10 美元。

02:55.739 --> 02:58.739
- Oh, ho ho,
I'd be stupid not to.
- 哦，嗬嗬，
我要是不这么做就太傻了。

02:58.739 --> 03:00.739
- Well, you're half right.
- 嗯，你说对了一半。

03:00.739 --> 03:02.139
- Here's your 20 bucks.
- 这是你的 20 美元。

03:02.139 --> 03:04.039
- Here's your glasses.
- Thanks.
- 这是你的眼镜。
- 谢谢。

03:04.039 --> 03:08.472
I'll take one Executive
Treatment, my good man.
我会选一名行政人员
治疗吧，我的好人。

03:08.472 --> 03:11.639
- Here's your
Executive Treatment.
- 这是你的
行政待遇。

03:11.639 --> 03:13.372
- Here you go.
- 干得好。

03:13.372 --> 03:14.839
- Oh, man.
- 哦，伙计。

03:14.839 --> 03:17.305
That looks
executively delicious.
看起来
行政美味。

03:17.305 --> 03:18.772
- Carl, what are you doing
standing around
- 卡尔，你在做什么
站在周围

03:18.772 --> 03:20.472
at a time like this?
在这样的时候？

03:20.472 --> 03:22.339
We're gonna be late for
the big brainstorming meeting.
我们要迟到了
大型头脑风暴会议。

03:22.339 --> 03:25.072
all: Business. Business.
Business. Business.
全体：商业。商业。
商业。商业。

03:25.072 --> 03:27.739
- Save my sandwich
for me, Squidward!
- 保存我的三明治
为了我，章鱼哥！

03:27.739 --> 03:29.739
Squidward!
章鱼哥！

03:29.739 --> 03:32.072
- Ah, I'll save it all right.
- 啊，我会保存它的。

03:32.072 --> 03:34.805
I'll just put it here
in the circular file.
我就把它放在这里
在循环文件中。

03:34.805 --> 03:37.405
[giggles]
[咯咯笑]

03:37.405 --> 03:38.805
- What are you doing
throwing away
- 你在做什么
扔掉

03:38.805 --> 03:41.305
a perfectly sellable sandwich?
一个非常畅销的三明治？

03:41.305 --> 03:44.939
all: Business.
Business. Business.
全体：商业。
商业。商业。

03:44.939 --> 03:47.772
- No!
Oh, no!
- 不！
哦，不！

03:47.772 --> 03:49.272
all: Business.
Business. Business.
全体：商业。
商业。商业。

03:49.272 --> 03:51.639
Business, business, business,
business, business.
商业、商业、商业、
生意，生意。

03:51.639 --> 03:53.239
- [straining]
- [紧张]

03:53.239 --> 03:57.172
all: Business, business,
business, business.
全部： 商业、商业、
生意，生意。

03:57.172 --> 03:59.872
- No!
- 不！

03:59.872 --> 04:02.872
[soft jazz music]
[轻柔的爵士乐]

04:02.872 --> 04:07.039
*
*
*
*
*
*
*
*

04:07.939 --> 04:09.739
[bell dings]
No!
[铃声]
不！

04:09.739 --> 04:13.439
all: Business. Business.
全体：商业。商业。

04:13.439 --> 04:15.805
- Not 4B!
- 不是4B！

04:15.805 --> 04:18.739
No!
不！

04:18.739 --> 04:21.339
- Wow, you're very upset
about Conference Room 4B.
- 哇，你很沮丧
关于 4B 会议室。

04:21.339 --> 04:23.739
And I can't say I blame you,
我不能说我责怪你

04:23.739 --> 04:25.139
because Conference Room 4B
因为4B会议室

04:25.139 --> 04:27.005
is the most terrifying
conference room
是最可怕的
会议室

04:27.005 --> 04:28.505
in the whole building.
在整个建筑中。

04:28.505 --> 04:30.739
More people have been
fired in here
更多人已经
在这里被发射

04:30.739 --> 04:33.339
than all the other
conference rooms combined.
比所有其他人
会议室合并。

04:33.339 --> 04:34.739
- [screams]
- [尖叫]

04:34.739 --> 04:36.639
- Save it for the big
brainstorming meeting.
- 保存为大
头脑风暴会议。

04:36.639 --> 04:39.605
Right here is where all
the biggest business decisions
一切都在这里
最大的商业决策

04:39.605 --> 04:41.272
in the business are made.
在业务中被制作。

04:41.272 --> 04:44.372
Why, if an imposter were
to be caught in here? Mm.
为什么，如果冒名顶替者是
会被抓到这里吗？毫米。

04:44.372 --> 04:47.172
- He'd be given a sandwich
and sent on his way?
- 他会得到一个三明治
并送上路？

04:47.172 --> 04:49.972
- No. He'd be convicted
as a corporate spy
- 不，他会被定罪
作为企业间谍

04:49.972 --> 04:52.739
and sent to jail forever
and ever and ever.
并被永远关进监狱
永远永远。

04:52.739 --> 04:54.005
Hey, where you going?
嘿，你要去哪里？

04:54.005 --> 04:56.005
- I think I forgot to...
- 我想我忘了...

04:56.005 --> 04:58.205
water my manatee.
I'll just--
给我的海牛浇水。
我就——

04:58.205 --> 05:02.139
- Gentlemen.
Ladies.
- 先生们。
女士们。

05:02.139 --> 05:03.505
- Where am I?
- 我在哪里？

05:03.505 --> 05:04.639
- Exactly.
- 确切地。

05:04.639 --> 05:05.972
I like you, young man.
我喜欢你，年轻人。

05:05.972 --> 05:08.305
Everybody scoot down
so he can sit next to me
大家赶紧下来
这样他就可以坐在我旁边

05:08.305 --> 05:09.639
and I won't intimidate him
at all
我不会恐吓他
根本不

05:09.639 --> 05:11.739
by my terrifying largeness
and proximity.
以我可怕的巨大
和接近度。

05:11.739 --> 05:14.772
As this junior executive
so eloquently put it,
正如这位初级管理人员
如此雄辩地说，

05:14.772 --> 05:16.572
where exactly are we?
我们到底在哪里？

05:16.572 --> 05:18.572
- Sir, if you take
a look at this,
- 先生，如果你接受
看看这个，

05:18.572 --> 05:20.505
I believe you'll agree that
we're perfectly positioned
我相信你会同意这一点
我们处于完美位置

05:20.505 --> 05:21.972
for our marketing
to be number one
为了我们的营销
成为第一

05:21.972 --> 05:23.205
across the business sector.
整个商业领域。

05:23.205 --> 05:25.139
all: Business.
Business. Business.
全体：商业。
商业。商业。

05:25.139 --> 05:26.305
- What I need is
a straight answer,
- 我需要的是
直接回答，

05:26.305 --> 05:28.405
not a bunch
of meaningless charts.
不是一堆
毫无意义的图表。

05:28.405 --> 05:30.072
What do you give
a disappointed stockholder
你给什么
失望的股东

05:30.072 --> 05:32.139
to make him feel better?
让他感觉好一点？

05:32.139 --> 05:34.739
- A sandwich?
- 三明治？

05:36.139 --> 05:38.272
[laughter]
[笑声]

05:38.272 --> 05:41.005
- Get a load of this guy!
A sandwich.
- 抓住这个家伙！
一个三明治。

05:41.005 --> 05:43.172
- This guy has sandwiches
on the brain.
- 这家伙有三明治
在大脑上。

05:43.172 --> 05:45.405
- No, I don't.
- 不，我不。

05:45.405 --> 05:48.005
- That's just about
the silliest piece of idea.
- 这只是关于
最愚蠢的想法。

05:48.005 --> 05:49.439
- All right, hold it.
- 好吧，坚持住。

05:49.439 --> 05:51.172
Now all of you just
hold it right there.
现在你们所有人都只是
把它放在那儿。

05:51.172 --> 05:54.372
It's easy to laugh and josh
and heap a man with scorn
开怀大笑很容易
并蔑视一个人

05:54.372 --> 05:56.005
when you hear an idea
that stands out
当你听到一个想法时
脱颖而出

05:56.005 --> 05:58.639
because it's so unusual.
因为它太不寻常了。

05:58.639 --> 06:00.272
So everybody just stop
and think for a minute
所以大家停下来
想一分钟

06:00.272 --> 06:03.072
about what your colleague here
is really trying to say.
关于你同事的事
真的很想说。

06:03.072 --> 06:05.205
Because I want to be the one
to tell him,
因为我想成为那个人
告诉他，

06:05.205 --> 06:07.272
"That's the silliest thing
I ever heard."
“这是最愚蠢的事情
我听说过。”

06:07.272 --> 06:09.872
- What if I have
a meaningless chart?
- 如果我有怎么办
无意义的图表？

06:09.872 --> 06:13.505
- Yes. Maybe I was
too hasty about that.
- 是的。也许我是
太仓促了。

06:13.505 --> 06:15.439
- Oh, good.
- 哦，很好。

06:18.772 --> 06:20.105
- Well, you've definitely
given new meaning
- 嗯，你肯定已经
被赋予新的意义

06:20.105 --> 06:22.039
to the word "meaningless."
到“无意义”这个词。

06:22.039 --> 06:23.372
- Oh, wait.
- 哦，等等。

06:24.839 --> 06:27.639
[chuckles]
[笑声]

06:27.639 --> 06:32.005
And here's a little house with
smoke coming out of the chimney.
这是一座小房子
烟从烟囱里冒出来。

06:32.005 --> 06:33.139
See what I mean?
明白我的意思吗？

06:33.139 --> 06:34.872
- [growls]
- [咆哮]

06:34.872 --> 06:37.005
- I guess he liked my chart.
He's smiling.
- 我猜他喜欢我的图表。
他在微笑。

06:37.005 --> 06:39.005
- He smiles like that
when he's really angry.
- 他笑起来就是这样
当他真的生气的时候。

06:39.005 --> 06:42.805
[all muttering in agreement]
- He does, does it every time.
[大家嘀咕着表示同意]
- 他确实这么做了，每次都这么做。

06:42.805 --> 06:46.105
- Do you slap your palms down
on the table like that, too?
- 你会拍手掌吗
桌子上也这样吗？

06:46.105 --> 06:49.739
- Yes.
- Oh.
- 是的。
- 哦。

06:49.739 --> 06:52.739
- I don't know who you are, but
you better not be an imposter.
- 我不知道你是谁，但是
你最好不要成为冒名顶替者。

06:52.739 --> 06:54.072
You know what happens
to imposters
你知道会发生什么
冒名顶替者

06:54.072 --> 06:55.739
in Conference Room 4B?
在4B会议室？

06:55.739 --> 06:58.339
- Well, uh, let's see.
Don't tell me.
- 嗯，让我们看看。
别告诉我。

06:58.339 --> 07:01.305
I know it's not sandwiches.
我知道这不是三明治。

07:01.305 --> 07:04.605
They don't get sandwiches.
Do they?
他们不吃三明治。
他们有吗？

07:08.139 --> 07:11.139
- Mister, this is
the last straw.
- 先生，这是
最后一根稻草。

07:11.139 --> 07:12.872
all: Aww.
全体：哇。

07:12.872 --> 07:16.039
- I'm going to give you just 18
more chances to prove yourself.
- 我只给你18
更多的机会证明自己。

07:16.039 --> 07:18.572
narrator: Montage.
旁白：蒙太奇。

07:18.572 --> 07:21.372
- [mumbling]
- [咕哝]

07:23.739 --> 07:25.539
- [growls]
- [咆哮]

07:25.539 --> 07:26.505
[all gasp]
[全都喘气]

07:26.505 --> 07:28.239
- Jenkins?
- Yes, sir.
- 詹金斯？
- 是的，先生。

07:28.239 --> 07:29.239
- Moustache.
- 胡子。

07:29.239 --> 07:31.805
- Ooh, here you are, sir.
- 哦，你在这里，先生。

07:57.005 --> 07:58.305
[timer dings]
[计时器的声音]

08:02.139 --> 08:04.605
- [whistles]
- [口哨]

08:24.272 --> 08:28.172
[drum roll]
[鼓声]

08:38.839 --> 08:40.739
And so in conclusion,
所以总而言之，

08:40.739 --> 08:44.305
I would like to submit
my official report.
我想提交
我的正式报告。

08:50.639 --> 08:53.605
- You know, kid, we need
somebody like you around here.
- 你知道，孩子，我们需要
这里有人像你一样。

08:53.605 --> 08:55.839
- You do?
- For me to fire.
- 你做？
- 让我开火。

08:55.839 --> 08:58.405
- Oh, yeah?
Well...
- 哦，是吗？
出色地...

08:58.405 --> 09:02.139
I've got
a surprise for you.
我有
给你一个惊喜。

09:02.139 --> 09:03.772
[all gasping]
- Where'd he go?
[全都喘气]
- 他去哪儿了？

09:03.772 --> 09:05.172
- You can't fire me.
- 你不能解雇我。

09:05.172 --> 09:07.805
I'm not an executive at all.
我根本不是行政人员。

09:07.805 --> 09:11.572
I'm just a guy
who happens to like sandwiches.
我只是个男人
谁碰巧喜欢三明治。

09:11.572 --> 09:13.272
So go ahead.
所以继续吧。

09:13.272 --> 09:17.739
Send me away forever as
a corporate spy if you want to,
将我永远送走
如果你愿意的话，可以当一名企业间谍

09:17.739 --> 09:21.539
but not before I've had my say.
但在我发表意见之前。

09:24.005 --> 09:27.339
[cell door clanks shut]
[牢房门叮当关上]

09:27.339 --> 09:29.839
[doors shut]
[门关上]

09:29.839 --> 09:31.272
- You have a visitor.
- 你有访客。

09:35.105 --> 09:36.372
- Who is it?
- 是谁？

09:36.372 --> 09:38.572
- Hello, Patrick.
- Hi, SpongeBob.
- 你好，帕特里克。
- 嗨，海绵宝宝。

09:38.572 --> 09:40.072
- Hey, I heard
you're in charge of
- 嘿，我听到了
你负责

09:40.072 --> 09:42.639
the laundry room on Thursdays.
That's nice.
周四去洗衣房。
那很好。

09:42.639 --> 09:43.739
- Yeah.
- 是的。

09:43.739 --> 09:46.772
Yeah, it's pretty nice, I guess.
是的，我想这很不错。

09:46.772 --> 09:49.205
- You know what that makes you?
- Uh-uh.
- 你知道这让你做什么吗？
- 呃呃。

09:49.205 --> 09:51.105
- An executive!
- 一位高管！

09:51.105 --> 09:53.305
- Oh, wait!
- 哦，等等！

09:53.305 --> 09:55.272
Is that what I think it is?
是我想的那样吗？

09:55.272 --> 09:57.872
- Uh-huh.
An Executive Treatment.
- 呃哈。
行政治疗。

10:00.239 --> 10:02.739
- [chomping]
- [咀嚼]

10:04.205 --> 10:06.639
Mmm.
嗯。

10:07.805 --> 10:11.239
Eh.
呃。

10:11.239 --> 10:12.472
- [gasps]
- [喘气]

10:12.472 --> 10:15.905
What happened
to prisoner 665321?
发生了什么
囚禁665321？

10:15.905 --> 10:20.272
[alarm blares]
[警报声]

10:20.272 --> 10:22.139
- Let's go home, SpongeBob.
- 我们回家吧，海绵宝宝。

10:22.139 --> 10:24.739
- Okay.
But who are you?
- 好的。
但你是谁？

10:24.739 --> 10:26.339
- [laughs]
- [笑]

10:26.339 --> 10:29.072
[laughter]
[笑声]

10:29.072 --> 10:32.272
Who am I?
我是谁？

10:32.272 --> 10:35.472
[laughter]
[笑声]

10:35.472 --> 10:37.605
- No, seriously, who are you?
- 不，说真的，你是谁？

- 不，说真的，你是谁？